{"complete":true,"school_name":"Gettysburg College","town_name":"Gettysburg","boards":[{"complete":true,"school_name":"Gettysburg College","town_name":"Gettysburg","template_id":"college-first-weekend","title":"Your First Weekend at Gettysburg College, Shared as Cards","description":"A conservative Friday-to-Sunday sequence for learning campus landmarks, finding student spaces, and connecting Gettysburg College with the surrounding history.","icon":"schedule","cards":[{"subject_id":"pennsylvania-hall","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Pennsylvania Hall","title":"Start at the College’s Historic Center","subtitle":"Friday afternoon · Pennsylvania Hall","notes":"Meet outside Penn Hall, identify its cupola and porticoes, and use this central landmark to orient yourself before exploring campus.","short_summary":"Begin with the original campus building and a dependable visual reference point.","evidence_claim":"Gettysburg College states that Pennsylvania Hall was built in 1837, was the original College building, and remains a focal point for Convocation and Commencement.","source_url":"https://www.gettysburg.edu/news/stories?Headline=Transformative+Places%2C+Resilient+Spaces&id=dee02b07-33e7-4ce6-985e-eed77423d127","source_title":"Transformative Places, Resilient Spaces","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2022-06-01","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Treat this as an exterior orientation stop; the building currently contains administrative offices.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"servo-dining-center","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Servo – The Dining Center","title":"Learn Your Main Dining Hall","subtitle":"Friday dinner · Servo","notes":"Use dinner to learn the serving areas, locate dietary selections, and practice entering with the student ID tied to your meal plan.","short_summary":"Get comfortable navigating the campus dining hall used by first-year meal plans.","evidence_claim":"Gettysburg College identifies the Dining Center as “Servo,” says it serves food seven days a week, and requires first-year students to maintain the Unlimited Servo Entry plan.","source_url":"https://www.gettysburg.edu/offices/dining-services/meal-plan-information/","source_title":"Meal Plans - Dining Services","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Operating hours vary; consult Dining Services before going. Entry uses a meal plan or another accepted payment method.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"cub-lobby","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"College Union Building Lobby","title":"Find the Campus Information Hub","subtitle":"Friday evening · College Union Building","notes":"Locate the information desk, scan the event displays, and try a lobby game while learning where student-service offices are housed.","short_summary":"Use the student union as a practical base for directions, services, and casual recreation.","evidence_claim":"The College says the CUB contains dining and student services; its lobby has board games, arcade games, video-game systems, a television, and a pool table.","source_url":"https://www.gettysburg.edu/offices/student-activities-greek-life/college-union-building/","source_title":"College Union Building","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The desk is staffed until 11 p.m. during semesters; students can enter the CUB 24/7 with their College ID.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"musselman-library","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Musselman Library","title":"Set Up Your Library Routine","subtitle":"Saturday morning · Musselman Library","notes":"Find the main service desk, charging lockers, and lower-level study room so you know where to return when coursework begins.","short_summary":"Map essential study and research services before the first busy academic week.","evidence_claim":"Musselman Library provides research assistance and offers a lower-level reservable study room plus charging lockers on its main level.","source_url":"https://www.gettysburg.edu/musselman-library/services/reserve-a-library-space","source_title":"Reserve A Library Space","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Room reservations are limited to College community members; building access after 8 p.m. requires a current College ID.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"schmucker-art-gallery","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Schmucker Art Gallery","title":"Add an Art Break","subtitle":"Saturday late morning · Schmucker Hall","notes":"Walk through the current exhibitions, note the gallery’s main-floor location, and check its calendar for future talks and programs.","short_summary":"Pair a campus walk with a changing exhibition in a publicly accessible gallery.","evidence_claim":"Schmucker Art Gallery is located on the main floor of Schmucker Hall and is free and open to the public Tuesday through Saturday, 10 a.m.–4 p.m.","source_url":"https://www.gettysburg.edu/offices/schmucker-art-gallery/","source_title":"Schmucker Art Gallery","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Open Tuesday–Saturday, 10 a.m.–4 p.m.; verify exhibition dates before visiting because installations change.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"jaeger-center","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"John F. Jaeger Center for Athletics, Recreation and Fitness","title":"Tour the Recreation Center","subtitle":"Saturday afternoon · Jaeger Center","notes":"Bring your student ID, locate the fitness and climbing areas, and review posted schedules before planning a first workout or swim.","short_summary":"Learn the layout of the College’s central recreation and fitness facility.","evidence_claim":"Gettysburg College describes the Jaeger Center as containing a fitness center, bouldering area, 30-foot climbing tower, fitness-class room, gym and natatorium.","source_url":"https://www.gettysburg.edu/accepted-students/glossary","source_title":"Gettysburg Glossary","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Student IDs are required for Jaeger Center access; consult the current Campus Recreation schedule before visiting.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"quarry-pavilion","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Quarry Pavilion","title":"Pause Beside Quarry Pond","subtitle":"Saturday late afternoon · West Campus","notes":"Walk to the pavilion in daylight, use its picnic tables for a group check-in, and note the nearby athletic fields for later events.","short_summary":"Take an outdoor pause at a named campus gathering place overlooking the pond.","evidence_claim":"Gettysburg College says Quarry Pavilion overlooks Quarry Pond, sits near athletic fields, and is equipped with picnic tables and charcoal grills.","source_url":"https://engage.gettysburg.edu/osagl/popular-campus-venues/","source_title":"Popular Campus Venues","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use during daylight and observe any posted reservation or event restrictions; grill use requires appropriate planning and supervision.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"majestic-theater","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Majestic Theater","title":"See What Is Playing Downtown","subtitle":"Saturday evening · 25 Carlisle Street","notes":"Check the official calendar, choose an age-appropriate film or performance, and buy through the theater’s site or box office only.","short_summary":"Connect campus with downtown through the College-owned historic theater.","evidence_claim":"The Majestic Theater says Gettysburg College purchased it in 1988; its official ticket page lists cinema and live-event sales at 25 Carlisle Street.","source_url":"https://www.gettysburgmajestic.org/tickets/","source_title":"Majestic Theater - Tickets","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Box-office hours are Monday–Friday 3–7:30 p.m., Saturday noon–7:30 p.m., and Sunday 1–5:30 p.m.; event times vary.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gettysburg-national-military-park","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Gettysburg National Military Park Museum and Visitor Center","title":"Begin the Battlefield Visit Indoors","subtitle":"Sunday morning · Gettysburg National Military Park","notes":"Start at the visitor center for orientation, ask what can be seen within your available time, and follow all bag-inspection rules.","short_summary":"Get official context and practical guidance before exploring the battlefield landscape.","evidence_claim":"The National Park Service identifies the Museum and Visitor Center as the place to begin a battlefield visit and lists daily seasonal operating hours.","source_url":"https://home.nps.gov/gett/planyourvisit/hours.htm","source_title":"Operating Hours & Seasons - Gettysburg National Military Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Open daily 8 a.m.–5 p.m. March–November and 9 a.m.–4 p.m. December–February; bags are subject to inspection.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"first-year-walk","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"First-Year Walk","title":"Understand the First-Year Walk Route","subtitle":"Sunday afternoon · Christ Chapel to the National Cemetery","notes":"Trace the documented route in daylight with friends, noting how campus connects to town and the National Cemetery before Orientation.","short_summary":"Close the weekend by learning the path of a documented Gettysburg College tradition.","evidence_claim":"Gettysburg College documents an annual First-Year Walk that begins at Christ Chapel, proceeds through town, and concludes at Gettysburg National Military Park.","source_url":"https://www.gettysburg.edu/news/stories?id=483bf34c-827a-48db-b783-6d29dc5c964c","source_title":"3 things to know about Orientation for the Class of 2027","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The official group walk occurs during Orientation; this card suggests learning the public route in daylight, not staging the ceremony independently.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
