our the Recreation Center","subtitle":"Saturday afternoon · Jaeger Center","notes":"Bring your student ID, locate the fitness and climbing areas, and review posted schedules before planning a first workout or swim.","short_summary":"Learn the layout of the College’s central recreation and fitness facility.","evidence_claim":"Gettysburg College describes the Jaeger Center as containing a fitness center, bouldering area, 30-foot climbing tower, fitness-class room, gym and natatorium.","source_url":"https://www.gettysburg.edu/accepted-students/glossary","source_title":"Gettysburg Glossary","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Student IDs are required for Jaeger Center access; consult the current Campus Recreation schedule before visiting.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"quarry-pavilion","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Quarry Pavilion","title":"Pause Beside Quarry Pond","subtitle":"Saturday late afternoon · West Campus","notes":"Walk to the pavilion in daylight, use its picnic tables for a group check-in, and note the nearby athletic fields for later events.","short_summary":"Take an outdoor pause at a named campus gathering place overlooking the pond.","evidence_claim":"Gettysburg College says Quarry Pavilion overlooks Quarry Pond, sits near athletic fields, and is equipped with picnic tables and charcoal grills.","source_url":"https://engage.gettysburg.edu/osagl/popular-campus-venues/","source_title":"Popular Campus Venues","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use during daylight and observe any posted reservation or event restrictions; grill use requires appropriate planning and supervision.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"majestic-theater","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Majestic Theater","title":"See What Is Playing Downtown","subtitle":"Saturday evening · 25 Carlisle Street","notes":"Check the official calendar, choose an age-appropriate film or performance, and buy through the theater’s site or box office only.","short_summary":"Connect campus with downtown through the College-owned historic theater.","evidence_claim":"The Majestic Theater says Gettysburg College purchased it in 1988; its official ticket page lists cinema and live-event sales at 25 Carlisle Street.","source_url":"https://www.gettysburgmajestic.org/tickets/","source_title":"Majestic Theater - Tickets","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Box-office hours are Monday–Friday 3–7:30 p.m., Saturday noon–7:30 p.m., and Sunday 1–5:30 p.m.; event times vary.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gettysburg-national-military-park","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Gettysburg National Military Park Museum and Visitor Center","title":"Begin the Battlefield Visit Indoors","subtitle":"Sunday morning · Gettysburg National Military Park","notes":"Start at the visitor center for orientation, ask what can be seen within your available time, and follow all bag-inspection rules.","short_summary":"Get official context and practical guidance before exploring the battlefield landscape.","evidence_claim":"The National Park Service identifies the Museum and Visitor Center as the place to begin a battlefield visit and lists daily seasonal operating hours.","source_url":"https://home.nps.gov/gett/planyourvisit/hours.htm","source_title":"Operating Hours & Seasons - Gettysburg National Military Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Open daily 8 a.m.–5 p.m. March–November and 9 a.m.–4 p.m. December–February; bags are subject to inspection.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"first-year-walk","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"First-Year Walk","title":"Understand the First-Year Walk Route","subtitle":"Sunday afternoon · Christ Chapel to the National Cemetery","notes":"Trace the documented route in daylight with friends, noting how campus connects to town and the National Cemetery before Orientation.","short_summary":"Close the weekend by learning the path of a documented Gettysburg College tradition.","evidence_claim":"Gettysburg College documents an annual First-Year Walk that begins at Christ Chapel, proceeds through town, and concludes at Gettysburg National Military Park.","source_url":"https://www.gettysburg.edu/news/stories?id=483bf34c-827a-48db-b783-6d29dc5c964c","source_title":"3 things to know about Orientation for the Class of 2027","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The official group walk occurs during Orientation; this card suggests learning the public route in daylight, not staging the ceremony independently.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
